{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jvia1Gy8TbxuX5eZaCqsGF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Execute and recover with TaskMesh\n2\t\n3\tInitialize TaskMesh with `taskspec mesh init` in the authorized host environment\n4\tbefore using it from a coding harness that protects Git metadata. Initialization\n5\twrites `.git/info/exclude` and creates the repository-local daemon state. Several\n6\tinspection commands also initialize a missing daemon; they are not guaranteed to\n7\tbe filesystem read-only. If the host denies this setup, report that boundary and\n8\twait for the required authorization. Do not switch tools to repeat the denied write.\n9\t\n10\tInspect `taskspec status <task>`, `taskspec mesh frontier`, and\n11\t`taskspec mesh explain --task <id>`. Ready leaves need a valid HMAC seal.\n12\tUse `taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> --execute` for the eligible native\n13\tinitiative frontier, or `mesh run --task <id> --execute` for one managed task.\n14\tDeclared resources and overlapping writes share the existing concurrency logic.\n15\tA run starts the currently eligible wave; inspect status before requesting later work.\n16\tWithout `--execute`, `mesh run` still creates a run, worktree and lease. Use\n17\t`--dry-run` for a preview; omitting `--execute` is not a preview.\n18\t\n19\tA recipe-managed run follows existing attempts, worktrees, leases, fencing,\n20\tcancellation, and recovery. Per-round artifacts retain executor and eval evidence;\n21\tno separate loop runner is introduced. In supervised mode, passing evals enter\n22\tawaiting_supervision.\n23\t\n24\tNew source worktrees live under `.taskspec/mesh/workspaces/<run>/`, outside Git's\n25\tmetadata directory. Existing recorded workspace paths remain valid. The daemon\n26\trenews the fenced lease while it owns an active executor; renewal does not extend\n27\tthe signed deadline or refund rounds. If renewal loses authority, execution stops.\n28\tRecognized harness permission-denial results park immediately instead of entering\n29\tanother repair round. Resolve the reported permission boundary before resuming;\n30\tan eval failure and a denied tool action need different recovery decisions.\n31\t\n32\tUse `mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>` only with\n33\tapplicable supervisor authorization. `finish` reports the human integration route.\n34\tCanonical acceptance receipts may already exist as untracked files in the\n35\tsupervisor checkout. After `finish`, inspect `git status --short` and commit the\n36\texact receipt files for that run before performing the reported merge. This\n37\tpreserves the evidence and avoids Git refusing to overwrite untracked receipts.\n38\tTaskMesh does not perform this user-branch commit or merge.\n39\t\n40\tAfter interruption, read `mesh status`, `mesh watch <run>`, and initiative state.\n41\tUse `mesh resume <run-or-attempt> --execute` only after resolving the recorded blocker.\n42\tResuming does not refund recipe rounds or restart its total deadline. Exhaustion\n43\trequires reviewed successor work, not silent budget expansion.\n44\t\n45\tOrdinary tasks retain direct `taskspec handoff`. Managed recipes require TaskMesh.\n46\tSupervised adapters and the attested OMP sandbox use the same round controller.\n47\tAutonomous OMP requires the pinned sandbox, fixed provider/model, external host\n48\tattestor, and evaluator trust registry. Each round receives a fresh expiring\n49\tcapability and retains its own signed execution evidence; prior credentials stay\n50\trevoked. Evals run in the sanitized host environment, and canonical acceptance\n51\treruns the task proof. Execution attestation does not claim eval isolation.\n52\tAutomatic acceptance evaluation uses the remaining signed deadline; cancellation\n53\talso stops its evaluator subprocesses. An explicit later supervisor acceptance\n54\tdoes not grant new execution rounds or reset the managed run's deadline.\n55\tCustom required environment contracts and hard token limits refuse before any\n56\tround when their enforcement cannot be established. No silent downgrade occurs.\n57\t\n58\tKeep the authorized task, native plan bundle, immutable snapshots, and applicable\n59\tsource evidence in the Git revision used for the attempt. Mesh creates worktrees\n60\tfrom that revision. Recording files in Git does not replace review or HMAC sealing.\n61\t\n62\tRound evidence distinguishes explicitly routed models from models reported by a\n63\tharness. Unreported defaults remain unknown; comparative qualification requires\n64\texplicit model and provider identities. Supervised adapters use the harness host\n65\tenvironment; required isolation or hard token enforcement must refuse if unavailable.\n66\t\n67\tRecipe-managed Claude runs with no declared MCP dependencies use restricted\n68\tRead/Edit/Write/Bash tools and an empty MCP configuration. User, project, and\n69\tlocal settings hooks are excluded from that worker context; managed host policy\n70\tstill applies. Explicit route model/provider choices remain authoritative.\n71\tDeclare needed MCP dependencies or provide an explicitly configured adapter.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715d9a2a-531c-4905-a73d-50ee4328be79","uuid":"2d26beeb-de12-4e16-85d6-7122e80f1a44","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:22:21.103Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat 9byg4ukv/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/execution.md","content":"# Execute and recover with TaskMesh\n\nInitialize TaskMesh with `taskspec mesh init` in the authorized host environment\nbefore using it from a coding harness that protects Git metadata. Initialization\nwrites `.git/info/exclude` and creates the repository-local daemon state. Several\ninspection commands also initialize a missing daemon; they are not guaranteed to\nbe filesystem read-only. If the host denies this setup, report that boundary and\nwait for the required authorization. Do not switch tools to repeat the denied write.\n\nInspect `taskspec status <task>`, `taskspec mesh frontier`, and\n`taskspec mesh explain --task <id>`. Ready leaves need a valid HMAC seal.\nUse `taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> --execute` for the eligible native\ninitiative frontier, or `mesh run --task <id> --execute` for one managed task.\nDeclared resources and overlapping writes share the existing concurrency logic.\nA run starts the currently eligible wave; inspect status before requesting later work.\nWithout `--execute`, `mesh run` still creates a run, worktree and lease. Use\n`--dry-run` for a preview; omitting `--execute` is not a preview.\n\nA recipe-managed run follows existing attempts, worktrees, leases, fencing,\ncancellation, and recovery. Per-round artifacts retain executor and eval evidence;\nno separate loop runner is introduced. In supervised mode, passing evals enter\nawaiting_supervision.\n\nNew source worktrees live under `.taskspec/mesh/workspaces/<run>/`, outside Git's\nmetadata directory. Existing recorded workspace paths remain valid. The daemon\nrenews the fenced lease while it owns an active executor; renewal does not extend\nthe signed deadline or refund rounds. If renewal loses authority, execution stops.\nRecognized harness permission-denial results park immediately instead of entering\nanother repair round. Resolve the reported permission boundary before resuming;\nan eval failure and a denied tool action need different recovery decisions.\n\nUse `mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>` only with\napplicable supervisor authorization. `finish` reports the human integration route.\nCanonical acceptance receipts may already exist as untracked files in the\nsupervisor checkout. After `finish`, inspect `git status --short` and commit the\nexact receipt files for that run before performing the reported merge. This\npreserves the evidence and avoids Git refusing to overwrite untracked receipts.\nTaskMesh does not perform this user-branch commit or merge.\n\nAfter interruption, read `mesh status`, `mesh watch <run>`, and initiative state.\nUse `mesh resume <run-or-attempt> --execute` only after resolving the recorded blocker.\nResuming does not refund recipe rounds or restart its total deadline. Exhaustion\nrequires reviewed successor work, not silent budget expansion.\n\nOrdinary tasks retain direct `taskspec handoff`. Managed recipes require TaskMesh.\nSupervised adapters and the attested OMP sandbox use the same round controller.\nAutonomous OMP requires the pinned sandbox, fixed provider/model, external host\nattestor, and evaluator trust registry. Each round receives a fresh expiring\ncapability and retains its own signed execution evidence; prior credentials stay\nrevoked. Evals run in the sanitized host environment, and canonical acceptance\nreruns the task proof. Execution attestation does not claim eval isolation.\nAutomatic acceptance evaluation uses the remaining signed deadline; cancellation\nalso stops its evaluator subprocesses. An explicit later supervisor acceptance\ndoes not grant new execution rounds or reset the managed run's deadline.\nCustom required environment contracts and hard token limits refuse before any\nround when their enforcement cannot be established. No silent downgrade occurs.\n\nKeep the authorized task, native plan bundle, immutable snapshots, and applicable\nsource evidence in the Git revision used for the attempt. Mesh creates worktrees\nfrom that revision. Recording files in Git does not replace review or HMAC sealing.\n\nRound evidence distinguishes explicitly routed models from models reported by a\nharness. Unreported defaults remain unknown; comparative qualification requires\nexplicit model and provider identities. Supervised adapters use the harness host\nenvironment; required isolation or hard token enforcement must refuse if unavailable.\n\nRecipe-managed Claude runs with no declared MCP dependencies use restricted\nRead/Edit/Write/Bash tools and an empty MCP configuration. User, project, and\nlocal settings hooks are excluded from that worker context; managed host policy\nstill applies. Explicit route model/provider choices remain authoritative.\nDeclare needed MCP dependencies or provide an explicitly configured adapter.\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
