{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019FVsbds1ycrH2VCMFXsksm","type":"tool_result","content":"mesh\n   mutation: optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\n\nstatus\n   mutation: none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n   usage: Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\n\ndecompose status\n   mutation: none\n   usage: Usage: taskspec decompose status <initiative>\n\nmesh init\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh init \n\nmesh doctor\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh doctor \n\nmesh serve\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh serve --foreground\n\nmesh frontier\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh frontier \n\nmesh run\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh run --task <id>|--frontier|--initiative <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>] [--provider <id>] [--mode supervised|autonomous] [--max-parallel <n>] [--execute]\n\nmesh status\n   mutation: uninitialized status is read-only; existing runtime inspection may restart its daemon\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh status [<run-or-attempt>]\n\nmesh watch\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh watch <run> [--after <sequence>]\n\nmesh explain\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh explain --task <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>]\n\nmesh cancel\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh cancel <attempt>\n\nmesh resume\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh resume <run-or-attempt> [--execute]\n\nmesh accept\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>\n\nmesh finish\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh finish <run>\n\nmesh adapters\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks; probe invokes adapter executables\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh adapters list|probe [<name>]\n\nmesh setup\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh setup sandbox\n\nmesh mcp\n   mutation: none\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh mcp","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715d9a2a-531c-4905-a73d-50ee4328be79","uuid":"d825df6a-de5c-4125-9209-ebb981e5393d","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:22:28.676Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"mesh\n   mutation: optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\n\nstatus\n   mutation: none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n   usage: Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\n\ndecompose status\n   mutation: none\n   usage: Usage: taskspec decompose status <initiative>\n\nmesh init\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh init \n\nmesh doctor\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh doctor \n\nmesh serve\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh serve --foreground\n\nmesh frontier\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh frontier \n\nmesh run\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh run --task <id>|--frontier|--initiative <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>] [--provider <id>] [--mode supervised|autonomous] [--max-parallel <n>] [--execute]\n\nmesh status\n   mutation: uninitialized status is read-only; existing runtime inspection may restart its daemon\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh status [<run-or-attempt>]\n\nmesh watch\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh watch <run> [--after <sequence>]\n\nmesh explain\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh explain --task <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>]\n\nmesh cancel\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh cancel <attempt>\n\nmesh resume\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh resume <run-or-attempt> [--execute]\n\nmesh accept\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>\n\nmesh finish\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh finish <run>\n\nmesh adapters\n   mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks; probe invokes adapter executables\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh adapters list|probe [<name>]\n\nmesh setup\n   mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh setup sandbox\n\nmesh mcp\n   mutation: none\n   usage: Usage: taskspec mesh mcp","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
